  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DACAAR activities in Afghanistan 2018-2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall objective:
Livelihoods, health and life quality improved on a sustainable basis for returnees, protracted IDPs and vulnerable host communities

The programme have six outcomes:
Outcome 1 (WASH):
Returnees, IDPs and their host communities have access to and use safe drinking water on a sustainable basis, with water points being operated and maintained by communities 
Outcome 2 (WASH):
Returnees, IDPs and their host communities have improved hygiene and sanitation behaviour and practices
Outcome 3 (WASH): 
WASH partners at national and sub-national level have improved capacity to implement successful  WASH interventions
Outcome 4 (Agriculture-based Natural Resources Management):
Vulnerable farmers and producers from among the returnees, IDPs and host communities have increased environmentally sustainable agricultural productivity and production
Outcome 5 (Employment and Business Creation):
Sustainable income-generating and livelihood opportunities for vulnerable youth have been created in a conflict sensitive manner, leading to jobs, income, and creation of small businesses.
Outcome 6 (Women&#x2019;s Empowerment):
Vulnerable women from among the returnees, IDPs and their host communities have access to social, and economic resources, and capacity to empower women</narrative>
  </description>
